Portions of the backend infrastructure and web console shell are adapted from Cwork
(https://github.com/SuruchBoss/Cwork), by the same author, under the same license.
Each adapted file says so in its header. Adapted so far, from Cwork commit 6e520ed:

  backend/src/core/config/        configuration, typed config tree, env validation
  backend/src/core/errors/        domain errors with stable codes
  backend/src/core/http/          exception filter; request-context middleware (x-request-id)
  backend/src/core/prisma/        Prisma service and module
  backend/test/                   end-to-end harness: global setup, database wipe guard, test app
  backend/Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, .github/workflows/ci.yml, eslint.config.mjs,
  prisma.config.ts, the Prisma schema conventions
  web/src/lib/                    API client (request/send/parse structure), ApiError, env
  web/src/app/                    layout, navigation, route guard, query client
  web/src/styles/                 design tokens and layout styles
  web/Dockerfile, web/nginx.conf, web/vite.config.ts, web/eslint.config.js

Adapted from Cwork commit 6e520ed for sign-in, users and roles (#4):

  backend/src/core/security/      crypto service (AES-256-GCM, Argon2id), permissions and roles,
                                  decorators, permissions guard, current user
  backend/src/core/http/pagination.dto.ts
  backend/src/modules/auth/       auth, MFA and JWT strategy and guard, user context, DTOs,
                                  password policy; domain/totp.ts and its tests copied unchanged
  backend/src/modules/audit/      audit service, controller and query
  backend/prisma/schema/          identity and audit models; the append-only audit trigger
  backend/prisma/seed.ts          the published demo second factor and the refusal to seed a
                                  database that is not a demo one
  web/src/stores/auth.store.ts    session store; web/src/lib/api-client.ts token refresh
  web/src/features/auth/          sign-in steps (password, second factor, enrolment)


